CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*i2c_adapter)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_adapter)...)
#421: FILE: drivers/gpu/drm/loongson/loongson_i2c.c:137:
+	i2c_adapter = kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_adapter), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

